{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"RoundTripREST"}],"role":"article","title":"REST cancellation and concurrency"},"abstract":[{"overridingTitle":"Documentation index","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Documentation index"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/RoundTripREST\/documentation\/RoundTripREST","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RestClient"},{"type":"text","text":" from async tasks and propagate cancellation from the caller. A cancelled URLSession operation may surface as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApiError.cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLError.cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" depending on the operation path."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkService.cancelAll()"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels all tasks in that service’s session. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalidate()"},{"type":"text","text":" also invalidates the session. Give separate features separate services when their cancellation lifetimes differ."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error publisher is a Combine value. Keep its subscriptions alive for as long as the observer needs them, and deliver UI changes on the main actor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RoundTripREST\/documentation\/RoundTripREST\/CancellationAndConcurrency","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RoundTripREST\/documentation\/RoundTripREST"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RoundTripREST\/documentation\/RoundTripREST\/RESTClient","doc:\/\/RoundTripREST\/documentation\/RoundTripREST\/ErrorsAndDecoding"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/do